{UTF-8}
{ Chapter 8: one input, six delays. Material delays (DELAY1, DELAY3, DELAY N, DELAY FIXED) and information delays (SMOOTH, SMOOTH3), all with the same average delay. }
Base Shipments=
	100
	~	cases/week
	~	Factory shipments before the test.
	|
Step Height=
	0
	~	cases/week
	~	Lasting rise in shipments at the test time.
	|
Pulse Volume=
	0
	~	cases
	~	A one-off extra load shipped during one week.
	|
Test Time=
	4
	~	week
	~	When the test input starts.
	|
Pulse Width=
	1
	~	week
	~	Duration of the extra load.
	|
Shipments=
	Base Shipments + STEP(Step Height, Test Time) + Pulse Volume * PULSE(Test Time, Pulse Width) / Pulse Width
	~	cases/week
	~	What leaves the factory each week.
	|
Delay Change=
	0
	~	week
	~	Reduction in the delay time from Change Time on.
	|
Change Time=
	20
	~	week
	~	When the delay time changes.
	|
Transit Time=
	6 - STEP(Delay Change, Change Time)
	~	week
	~	Average time in transit.
	|
Arrivals DELAY1=
	DELAY1(Shipments, Transit Time)
	~	cases/week
	~	First-order material delay.
	|
Arrivals DELAY3=
	DELAY3(Shipments, Transit Time)
	~	cases/week
	~	Third-order material delay.
	|
Arrivals DELAY12=
	DELAY N(Shipments, Transit Time, Base Shipments, 12)
	~	cases/week
	~	Twelfth-order material delay.
	|
Arrivals Fixed=
	DELAY FIXED(Shipments, 6, Base Shipments)
	~	cases/week
	~	Pipeline delay: every case takes exactly six weeks.
	|
Perceived SMOOTH=
	SMOOTH(Shipments, Transit Time)
	~	cases/week
	~	First-order information delay.
	|
Perceived SMOOTH3=
	SMOOTH3(Shipments, Transit Time)
	~	cases/week
	~	Third-order information delay.
	|
FINAL TIME = 60 ~ week ~ |
INITIAL TIME = 0 ~ week ~ |
SAVEPER = TIME STEP ~ week ~ |
TIME STEP = 0.0625 ~ week ~ |
